The '''Hassks''' were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] [[Homeworld|native]] to [[Hasskyn]]. They were almost completely covered in fur, except for their [[Color|gray]]-skinned faces. They had sensitive hearing and keen night vision, all the better for [[hunting]]. Hassk were near-feral, and were thought of by most as wild animals. They lived in a primitive culture with limited technology. When they were first confronted with [[Realspace|space]] travel, many left their homes and sought out worlds to wreak havoc, particularly in places of ill repute. A number of Hassks came to join [[Kragan Gorr]]'s [[Warbird gang|pirate gang]]. The [[Hassk triplets]] were thugs who spent time at [[Takodana Castle]] stirring up trouble.

==Biology and appearance==
Hassks were a [[species]] of [[subhumanoid]]s [[Homeworld|native]] to [[Hasskyn]].<ref name="Alien Archive" /> Their bodies were almost entirely covered with [[Color|cream-colored]] [[Hair|fur]]. Their faces, however, were hairless, revealing grey<ref name="TFAVD" /> or cornflower blue skin.<ref name="Synara's Score" /> They had sensitive [[ear]]s, two large forward-facing [[eye]]s that could be orange in hue and gave them a keen night vision. Their [[mouth]]s were filled with flesh-tearing [[Tooth|fangs]]<ref name="TFAVD" /> and had powerful jaws that could cause serious damage.<ref name="VE">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref>

==Society and culture==
[[File:Cantina-Hassk-SWCT.png|thumb|left|180px|One of the Hassk triplets having a drink in Maz Kanata's castle]]
Despite being [[Sentience|sentient]], the Hassks had a fierce behavior, suggestive of wild animals,<ref name="TFAVD" /> and their culture was primitive. Multiple [[Reproduction|births]] were known to occur among them, with the siblings being referred to as littermates.<ref name="Topps Hasks">{{Topps|set=2015 Topps Star Wars: The Force Awakens Series 1|cardname=Hassk Triplets}}</ref>

==Hassks in the galaxy==
When they were first confronted with advanced technology, the Hassks were not prepared for its impact on morality. Consequently, many of them left Hasskyn to roam [[the galaxy]] with their littermates, making trouble in places of ill repute.<ref name="Topps Hasks" />

One Hassk was serving as a member of the [[Gray Gundarks]] [[speeder bike]] gang when they attempted to claim the lost treasure of the [[Sith Lord]] [[Count]] [[Dooku]] on the [[planet]] [[Ponemah Terminal]] sometime after the [[Battle of Endor]].<ref name="TCC">"[[The Crimson Corsair and the Lost Treasure of Count Dooku]]"</ref>

A number of Hassk [[pirate]]s including [[Tooms]] and [[Snarl]] served as members of [[Kragan Gorr]]'s [[Warbird gang|pirate gang]] during the [[New Republic era|era]] of the [[New Republic]].<ref name="The Triple Dark">{{Resistance|The Triple Dark}}</ref><ref name="Signal from Sector Six">{{Resistance|Signal from Sector Six}}</ref><ref name="Synara's Score" />

[[Varmik]] and his two siblings, the [[Hassk triplets]], were known to attend the [[Takodana Castle|castle]] of the [[pirate]] [[Maz Kanata]] around thirty [[Standard year|years]] after the [[Battle of Endor]]. While those thugs often attempted to create mischief in the castle's main hall, other beings kept the peace.<ref name="TFAVD" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Strono_no_mask.png|thumb|right|250px|[[Paul Warren]] ([[Varmik]]) and [[Aidan Cook]] ([[Strono Tuggs]]) ''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'' rehearsals.]]
The Hassk species first appeared in the junior novel ''[[Smuggler's Run: A Han Solo & Chewbacca Adventure]]'',<ref name="Smuggler's Run">''[[Smuggler's Run: A Han Solo & Chewbacca Adventure]]''</ref> which was written by [[Greg Rucka]] and released on [[September 4]], [[2015]].<ref name="Disney">{{Disney|subdomain=books|url=book/smugglers-run|text=Smuggler's Run: A Han Solo Adventure}}</ref> They were created for the scenes in Takodana Castle in the film [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']] and were conceived by artist [[Ivan Manzella]], based upon a [[1975]] [[Chalmun's Spaceport Cantina|cantina]] illustration and an older [[Chewbacca]] concept by [[Ralph McQuarrie]]. They were designed by Manzella as a maquette under the name "Maz's Castle Alien c069" in December [[2013]].<ref name="Art of">''[[The Art of Star Wars: The Force Awakens]]''</ref>

